
# <type>(<scope>): <subject>


# --- RULES -----------------------------------------------------------
# Type MUST be one of:
#   feat:     A new feature
#   fix:      A bug fix
#   docs:     Documentation only changes
#   style:    Formatting, semicolons, etc (no code change)
#   refactor: Code change that neither fixes a bug nor adds a feature
#   perf:     Performance improvement
#   test:     Adding or updating tests
#   build:    Build system or dependencies (nix, npm, cargo)
#   ci:       CI/CD configuration
#   chore:    Maintenance tasks (tooling, configs)
#   revert:   Reverts a previous commit
#
# Scope is optional: module, file, or area affected
#   Examples: nvim, hyprland, k3s, shell, git
#
# Subject: imperative mood, lowercase, no period, max 50 chars
#   Good:  "add OAuth2 login support"
#   Bad:   "Added OAuth2 login support."
#
# Body (optional): explain WHAT and WHY, wrap at 72 chars
#
# Footer (optional): reference issues, BREAKING CHANGE
#   BREAKING CHANGE: <description>
#   Closes #123
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------
